VALUES (623, '1', 'ASK 623: Gemini 4 Hydrogen and Gemini 4 Neon debate and judge',
  $t$The operator can choose Gemini 4 Neon or Gemini 4 Hydrogen as either debater, and can place each as a panel judge or an alternate on the Judge order page. Both seats stand under every rule that binds the present seats: no judge of a debater's family; no judge running a debater's model (ASK 601); the enforcer never of a debater's family (ASK 608); a panel of exactly three. LIVE on write (ruling 512). (plan rev 0, OBJECTIVE, ask623/w4/plan623.md 87989e36)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 16:01 CST 2026-11-24 on the card "Write it" in W4's thread (Wall 11742; audit 41709). Database, in one transaction: a new model_config row neon (google/gemini-4-neon, family google, no reasoning field; the hydrogen row unchanged); neon added to the seat list of odv1_record_panel_substitution and to dash_judge_lineup, dash_odv1_debates and dash_odv1_judges; hydrogen and neon added to dash_debaters (the launch list, now 12 debaters); hydrogen and neon appended to the judge order as alternates 6 and 7 with a log row. Engine 0d55aab1 to 20db58ee-a005-4ecc-8313-258833c915a7, five nodes, seat tables only: Init Seats (the debater list gains hydrogen and neon; the family table and JFAM gain neon), Resolve Seats, Build Synthesis, Build Independent Verdict and Build Diagnostic Prompt (JFAM gains neon). Child and Library untouched; no prompt text changed; no reasoning or effort setting added; nothing deleted. W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11743). The engine manual entry was written by W3 at 16:27 CST on its own card (part 10.0 v310; Wall 11754; audit 41725; W1 readback MATCH, Wall 11755). Shown offline: 132 pairings, 128 seat three judges and 4 stop with the ASK 608 reason as before; on the 90 present pairings no judge, reserve or enforcer changes (68 change only in the tail of the alternates list); Neon against Hydrogen is judged by sol62, spark and sol with luna enforcing; the 8 new pairings of a Google debater against chatgpt or sol62 seat spark, qwen4max and sonnet with glm enforcing and have no reserve and no alternate, so 12 pairings now have none. Each model returned a complete debate answer in one paid check call with no reasoning setting (Hydrogen execution 42337, Neon execution 42339; 0.369 dollars together). Departures from what was pressed, both stated to the operator: the plan card's default "neither placed in the judge order until you save it" could not work, because the Judge order page cannot add a seat, so he pressed to append both; and the judge order reads version 5, not 3 as the write card said, because two rolled-back dry runs used log ids 3 and 4 (the order's contents are as pressed). As alternates the two seats can be offered a removed judge's seat with no Save, after the alternates ahead of them. Not shown by a run: neither seat has debated under its own name, the engine has never called neon in any role, and no run has been made since the write. Open: each seat in a live run in each role, two clean live runs per path (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24).$t$,
  '11705, 11706, 11708, 11712, 11715, 11716, 11734, 11735, 11737, 11742, 11743, 11746, 11748, 11751, 11754, 11755',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$The operator's part is four card presses and one answer. (1) The plan card in W3's thread, "Plan ASK 623 for Neon and Hydrogen as drafted?" (card cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo586NpWMro9hCDri3RvKxfiUu): he pressed "Plan it as drafted" at 14:48 CST 2026-11-24 (md_notes_rulings row 541 of seat 33). The option's words: "W4 plans: Hydrogen from its present row (65,536), Neon at 64,000, no reasoning setting, neither placed in the judge order until you save it." The other choices were "Plan it, both at 64,000", "Change something else" and "Hold". (2) W4's card on the judge order and the two paid check calls (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo585tYRKA3TeKEKRbVQv4FaKb): he pressed its first option at 15:01 CST; W4's notes623.md and W4's checklist give the option as "Append both; run the 2 checks". W3 did not read the card's question text. (3) To W4's question whether it may read the n8n output of the two check executions, those two only, if a reply is cut off, he first wrote at 15:35 CST: "as mentioned in the operation doc ... when asking me a question either enumerate or place on a separate line clearly asking a question do not embed." W4 asked again as an enumerated question, and he answered at 15:35 CST: "1" (option 1: "Yes: I run both check calls now."). (4) W4's write card "Write ASK 623 (Neon and Hydrogen seats) to live now?" (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo586qaQ3rcrUixFPWZFXcZdZe): he pressed "Write it" at 16:01 CST. (5) W3's manual card "Write the engine manual entries for ASK 607 and ASK 623?" (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58HchLDxYapz2pmrm9hZXW9c): he pressed "Write both entries" at 16:24 CST (md_notes_rulings row 547 of seat 33).$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write ASK 623 (Neon and Hydrogen seats) to live now?", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo586qaQ3rcrUixFPWZFXcZdZe", "press_time": "16:01 CST 2026-11-24 (22:01:02Z)", "source": "the card and its press read by W3 in W4's thread; Wall 11742; audit 41709", "plan_card": {"card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo586NpWMro9hCDri3RvKxfiUu", "question": "Plan ASK 623 for Neon and Hydrogen as drafted?", "answer": "Plan it as drafted", "press_time": "14:48 CST 2026-11-24", "thread": "W3", "source": "md_notes_rulings row 541 of seat 33; Wall 11712"}, "order_and_check_card": {"card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo585tYRKA3TeKEKRbVQv4FaKb", "answer": "Append both; run the 2 checks (the first option; label from notes623.md)", "press_time": "15:01 CST 2026-11-24 (21:01:31Z)", "thread": "W4", "source": "the press read by W3 in W4's thread; notes623.md; the question text not read by W3"}, "fallback_read": {"answer": "1", "press_time": "15:35 CST 2026-11-24 (21:35:53Z)", "thread": "W4", "message_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58SXynZgKxN4WNCVB55foqMc", "note": "a typed answer to W4's enumerated question, limited to the two check executions", "source": "read by W3 in W4's thread; Wall 11734"}, "manual_card": {"card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58HchLDxYapz2pmrm9hZXW9c", "question": "Write the engine manual entries for ASK 607 and ASK 623?", "answer": "Write both entries", "press_time": "16:24 CST 2026-11-24", "thread": "W3", "source": "md_notes_rulings row 547 of seat 33"}}$j$::jsonb,
